div.p:
4. Thou no longer talkest of thy goods or thy fruits, knowing they are not thine, but God’s. The earth is the Lord’s, and the fullness thereof;
Ps. 24:1. he is the proprietor of heaven and earth. He cannot divest himself of his glory: he must be the Lord, the possessor of all that is. Only he hath left a portion of his goods in thy hands, for such uses as he has specified. How long he will be pleased to lodge them with thee thou dost not yet know, perhaps only till tomorrow, or tonight. Therefore talk not, think not, of many years. Knowest thou not that thou art a creature of a day, that art crushed before the moth?
Job 4:19; see also No. 54, ‘On Eternity’, §6. That the breath which is in thy nostrils may be taken away at a moment’s warning? That it may be resumed by him that gave it, at a time thou thinkest not of it? How knowest thou but the next time thou liest down on thy bed thou mayest hear, ‘This night shall thy soul be required of thee’?
